# D2-WORX Environment Variables — Non-Secret Config
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# WARNING: Never commit .env.local to version control.
#
# SPLIT:
#   - Non-secret config (URLs, ports, container names, image tags, feature flags) → THIS FILE (.env.local)
#   - Secrets (passwords, API keys, third-party tokens, embedded-cred URLs) → .env.secrets (template: .env.secrets.example)
#
# Compose loads BOTH files; .env.secrets overrides .env.local on collision.
# See: docker compose -f infra/compose/compose.yml --env-file .env.local --env-file .env.secrets ...
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for non-secret configuration.
# Code reads env vars with NO defaults — if a required var is missing, it crashes.
#
# Convention: SERVICE_LAYER__PROPERTY (double underscore = hierarchy separator).
# .NET AddEnvironmentVariables() auto-maps __ to : for IConfiguration binding.
#
# DOCKER COMPOSE OVERRIDES:
# Values marked [DOCKER OVERRIDE] use localhost for host-side tooling (tests, debugger).
# infra/compose/compose.yml `environment:` replaces these with Docker DNS names at runtime
# (e.g., localhost:54320 → d2-postgres:5432).

# ===========================================
# Credentials
# ===========================================
# All credentials (usernames + passwords + sender identities) live in .env.secrets
# so related fields stay grouped together. See .env.secrets.example.

